1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,231
Release one point four of the orders service will not ship.

2
00:00:04,231 --> 00:00:05,179
The tests fail.

3
00:00:05,179 --> 00:00:06,634
The jar will not start.

4
00:00:06,634 --> 00:00:09,795
And your manager asks one question: what is wrong,

5
00:00:09,795 --> 00:00:11,060
and how do you know?

6
00:00:11,610 --> 00:00:14,663
This is the mastery lesson for Java fundamentals.

7
00:00:14,663 --> 00:00:16,533
You have learned eight skills.

8
00:00:16,533 --> 00:00:18,963
Now you prove them on a broken release,

9
00:00:18,963 --> 00:00:19,649
with a lab,

10
00:00:19,649 --> 00:00:20,272
a checker,

11
00:00:20,272 --> 00:00:21,082
and a report.

12
00:00:21,632 --> 00:00:24,597
I will fix the first fault live. You fix the other three.

13
00:00:26,647 --> 00:00:28,084
Meet the orders service,

14
00:00:28,084 --> 00:00:29,760
one build away from release.

15
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:30,778
Here is its path,

16
00:00:30,778 --> 00:00:32,514
with a red pin on each fault.

17
00:00:33,064 --> 00:00:33,534
Pin one,

18
00:00:33,534 --> 00:00:37,300
in the tests: the total subtracts shipping instead of adding it.

19
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:38,653
That is a failing test.

20
00:00:39,203 --> 00:00:39,706
Pin two,

21
00:00:39,706 --> 00:00:41,781
in the jar: it has no main class,

22
00:00:41,781 --> 00:00:44,108
so Java does not know where to start.

23
00:00:44,108 --> 00:00:45,240
That is packaging.

24
00:00:45,790 --> 00:00:46,392
Pin three,

25
00:00:46,392 --> 00:00:48,977
in the settings file: the port says eighty,

26
00:00:48,977 --> 00:00:49,638
in letters,

27
00:00:49,638 --> 00:00:50,420
not a number.

28
00:00:50,420 --> 00:00:51,742
That is configuration.

29
00:00:52,292 --> 00:00:52,837
Pin four,

30
00:00:52,837 --> 00:00:55,921
in the launcher: the heap limit is eight megabytes,

31
00:00:55,921 --> 00:00:57,977
and the catalog needs twenty-four.

32
00:00:57,977 --> 00:00:58,884
That is memory.

33
00:00:59,434 --> 00:01:03,317
The checker prints pass or fail for six checks, and all six fail.

34
00:01:03,867 --> 00:01:07,174
Your mission: six pass lines, with proof for every fix.

35
00:01:09,224 --> 00:01:13,427
Before we start, here is where everything lives. It is also in the description.

36
00:01:13,977 --> 00:01:19,651
The repository is git hub dot com, slash it dash waves, slash dev ops dash A I.

37
00:01:20,201 --> 00:01:23,193
The lab is one file: lab eighty-four dot S H,

38
00:01:23,193 --> 00:01:24,789
with its shortcuts file,

39
00:01:24,789 --> 00:01:26,917
in the academy slash lab folder.

40
00:01:26,917 --> 00:01:32,169
Your report template and install notes are in academy slash lesson eighty-four.

41
00:01:32,719 --> 00:01:34,600
Install it in three steps.

42
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:36,119
Clone the repository.

43
00:01:36,119 --> 00:01:37,638
Go to the lab folder.

44
00:01:37,638 --> 00:01:41,978
Install the script into slash U S R slash local slash S bin.

45
00:01:42,528 --> 00:01:44,496
Three commands run everything.

46
00:01:44,496 --> 00:01:46,662
Lab up builds the broken release.

47
00:01:46,662 --> 00:01:49,615
Lab check prints pass or fail for each check.

48
00:01:49,615 --> 00:01:51,189
Lab down removes it all.

49
00:01:51,739 --> 00:01:53,107
Lab is a short name.

50
00:01:53,107 --> 00:01:54,884
Source the shortcuts file,

51
00:01:54,884 --> 00:01:56,935
shortcuts eighty-four dot S H,

52
00:01:56,935 --> 00:01:58,234
and it runs sue do,

53
00:01:58,234 --> 00:01:59,875
lab eighty-four dot S H,

54
00:01:59,875 --> 00:02:00,422
for you.

55
00:02:00,972 --> 00:02:06,775
You need an Ubuntu virtual machine with root and a J D K. Run it only in your own machine.

56
00:02:09,125 --> 00:02:10,057
Now for real.

57
00:02:10,057 --> 00:02:12,136
I have cloned the repository,

58
00:02:12,136 --> 00:02:15,361
and the lab files are in a folder called lab.

59
00:02:15,361 --> 00:02:16,006
Type: CD,

60
00:02:16,006 --> 00:02:16,293
lab.

61
00:02:16,843 --> 00:02:18,998
List what is here. Type: L S.

62
00:02:19,548 --> 00:02:22,549
The lab script and the shortcuts file.

63
00:02:22,549 --> 00:02:24,049
Install the script.

64
00:02:24,049 --> 00:02:25,076
Type: sue do,

65
00:02:25,076 --> 00:02:25,708
install,

66
00:02:25,708 --> 00:02:26,260
dash m,

67
00:02:26,260 --> 00:02:27,524
seven five five,

68
00:02:27,524 --> 00:02:29,419
lab eighty-four dot S H,

69
00:02:29,419 --> 00:02:32,262
slash U S R slash local slash S bin.

70
00:02:32,812 --> 00:02:37,484
Load the short names. Type: source, shortcuts eighty-four dot S H.

71
00:02:38,034 --> 00:02:40,061
Build the lab. Type: lab up.

72
00:02:42,611 --> 00:02:45,192
Now ask the checker. Type: lab check.

73
00:02:46,742 --> 00:02:50,902
Six FAIL lines. That is your starting point. Copy them into your report.

74
00:02:52,952 --> 00:02:54,701
Keep four notes for every fault.

75
00:02:55,251 --> 00:02:58,387
One: the symptom, in the exact words of the output.

76
00:02:58,937 --> 00:03:01,369
Two: the cause, and the command that proved it.

77
00:03:01,919 --> 00:03:04,202
Three: the fix. One change only.

78
00:03:04,752 --> 00:03:07,184
Four: the proof, the output after the fix.

79
00:03:07,734 --> 00:03:09,889
Notes turn a lucky fix into evidence.

80
00:03:11,939 --> 00:03:12,659
Fault one,

81
00:03:12,659 --> 00:03:13,018
live.

82
00:03:13,018 --> 00:03:15,393
The checker says the build fails.

83
00:03:15,393 --> 00:03:16,904
Go to the lab folder.

84
00:03:16,904 --> 00:03:17,551
Type: CD,

85
00:03:17,551 --> 00:03:18,271
slash opt,

86
00:03:18,271 --> 00:03:19,854
slash lab eighty-four.

87
00:03:20,404 --> 00:03:23,732
Run the build. Type: S H, build dot S H.

88
00:03:25,282 --> 00:03:25,896
Note one,

89
00:03:25,896 --> 00:03:26,715
the symptom.

90
00:03:26,715 --> 00:03:29,309
Two tests fail: expected twelve fifty,

91
00:03:29,309 --> 00:03:30,402
got seven fifty.

92
00:03:30,402 --> 00:03:31,767
And the build stops.

93
00:03:32,317 --> 00:03:37,672
Where is the total calculated? Type: grep -n SHIPPING src/cloudcart/Orders.java

94
00:03:37,802 --> 00:03:39,932
Line eight: price times quantity,

95
00:03:39,932 --> 00:03:40,900
minus shipping.

96
00:03:40,900 --> 00:03:41,481
Note two,

97
00:03:41,481 --> 00:03:43,030
the cause: it subtracts.

98
00:03:43,030 --> 00:03:44,192
The test is right.

99
00:03:44,192 --> 00:03:45,354
The code is wrong.

100
00:03:45,904 --> 00:03:46,993
Note three,

101
00:03:46,993 --> 00:03:47,784
the fix.

102
00:03:47,784 --> 00:03:49,368
One change only.

103
00:03:49,368 --> 00:03:55,802
Type: sed -i 's/- SHIPPING/+ SHIPPING/' src/cloudcart/Orders.java

104
00:03:55,932 --> 00:04:00,434
Note four, the proof. Build again. Type: S H, build dot S H.

105
00:04:02,484 --> 00:04:04,916
Both tests pass, and the jar is built.

106
00:04:05,466 --> 00:04:10,052
Now run the service. Type: S H, run dash orders dot S H.

107
00:04:12,102 --> 00:04:13,894
It fails, and points to the log.

108
00:04:14,444 --> 00:04:19,351
Read the top of the log. Type: head -2 logs/orders.log

109
00:04:19,481 --> 00:04:21,237
No main manifest attribute.

110
00:04:21,237 --> 00:04:22,538
The symptom changed,

111
00:04:22,538 --> 00:04:25,464
and that is progress: this is the next fault,

112
00:04:25,464 --> 00:04:26,180
in the jar.

113
00:04:26,730 --> 00:04:29,311
Now ask the checker. Type: lab check.

114
00:04:29,861 --> 00:04:30,443
One PASS,

115
00:04:30,443 --> 00:04:31,090
five FAIL.

116
00:04:31,090 --> 00:04:32,060
One fault down,

117
00:04:32,060 --> 00:04:32,771
one change,

118
00:04:32,771 --> 00:04:33,482
with proof.

119
00:04:33,482 --> 00:04:36,069
Now it is your turn for the other three.

120
00:04:38,119 --> 00:04:41,895
Your report has five parts. The template is in the lesson folder.

121
00:04:42,445 --> 00:04:44,578
Setup: the checker output at the start.

122
00:04:45,128 --> 00:04:46,750
Each fault, with its four notes.

123
00:04:47,300 --> 00:04:50,393
The final checker output, with six lines saying pass.

124
00:04:50,943 --> 00:04:52,071
Where you got stuck,

125
00:04:52,071 --> 00:04:53,256
and what unstuck you.

126
00:04:53,256 --> 00:04:56,020
Honest notes are worth more than a perfect story.

127
00:04:56,570 --> 00:04:58,640
And the cleanup proof, which we do next.

128
00:04:59,190 --> 00:05:01,416
The lab also wants one short file,

129
00:05:01,416 --> 00:05:02,463
report dot text,

130
00:05:02,463 --> 00:05:04,427
in the lab folder: four lines,

131
00:05:04,427 --> 00:05:05,344
one per fault,

132
00:05:05,344 --> 00:05:06,392
naming the test,

133
00:05:06,392 --> 00:05:07,243
the manifest,

134
00:05:07,243 --> 00:05:07,832
the port,

135
00:05:07,832 --> 00:05:08,683
and the heap.

136
00:05:10,633 --> 00:05:11,809
Your three faults.

137
00:05:11,809 --> 00:05:12,592
No spoilers,

138
00:05:12,592 --> 00:05:13,637
only directions.

139
00:05:13,637 --> 00:05:14,682
After every fix,

140
00:05:14,682 --> 00:05:15,335
run again,

141
00:05:15,335 --> 00:05:18,078
because the next symptom is the next clue.

142
00:05:18,628 --> 00:05:19,333
Fault two,

143
00:05:19,333 --> 00:05:19,897
the jar.

144
00:05:19,897 --> 00:05:22,434
List its manifest with unzip dash P.

145
00:05:22,434 --> 00:05:24,618
If there is no main class line,

146
00:05:24,618 --> 00:05:27,437
the jar was made without an entry point.

147
00:05:27,437 --> 00:05:31,102
Rebuild it with the C F E option of the jar command,

148
00:05:31,102 --> 00:05:32,300
in build dot S H,

149
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:33,498
then build again.

150
00:05:34,048 --> 00:05:34,863
Fault three,

151
00:05:34,863 --> 00:05:35,747
the settings.

152
00:05:35,747 --> 00:05:38,873
The first line of the log names the exception,

153
00:05:38,873 --> 00:05:41,116
and the exact value it choked on.

154
00:05:41,116 --> 00:05:43,495
Fix that value in orders dot E N V,

155
00:05:43,495 --> 00:05:44,650
with one command.

156
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:45,935
Fault four,

157
00:05:45,935 --> 00:05:46,402
memory.

158
00:05:46,402 --> 00:05:49,005
The next log line says Java heap space.

159
00:05:49,005 --> 00:05:52,476
The limit is on the java opts line of the same file.

160
00:05:52,476 --> 00:05:53,077
Raise it,

161
00:05:53,077 --> 00:05:54,011
and run again.

162
00:05:54,561 --> 00:05:58,828
Same method every time: symptom, cause, fix one thing, verify.

163
00:06:00,878 --> 00:06:04,270
When you finish, clean up, and prove it. Type: lab down.

164
00:06:05,820 --> 00:06:11,196
Proof one: is the lab folder gone? Type: L S, slash opt, slash lab eighty-four.

165
00:06:11,746 --> 00:06:13,740
No such file or directory.

166
00:06:13,740 --> 00:06:15,810
Proof two: count it in opt.

167
00:06:15,810 --> 00:06:16,577
Type: L S,

168
00:06:16,577 --> 00:06:17,344
slash opt,

169
00:06:17,344 --> 00:06:17,727
pipe,

170
00:06:17,727 --> 00:06:18,647
grep dash c,

171
00:06:18,647 --> 00:06:19,874
lab eighty-four.

172
00:06:20,424 --> 00:06:22,963
Zero. Now remove the lab script itself.

173
00:06:23,513 --> 00:06:30,361
Type: sue do, R M, slash U S R slash local slash S bin slash lab eighty-four dot S H.

174
00:06:30,911 --> 00:06:34,107
Proof three: is anything left in S bin?

175
00:06:34,107 --> 00:06:34,926
Type: L S,

176
00:06:34,926 --> 00:06:37,877
slash U S R slash local slash S bin,

177
00:06:37,877 --> 00:06:38,287
pipe,

178
00:06:38,287 --> 00:06:38,614
W C,

179
00:06:38,614 --> 00:06:39,188
dash l.

180
00:06:39,738 --> 00:06:40,506
Zero.

181
00:06:41,056 --> 00:06:45,813
Proof four: is any Java still running? Type: P grep, dash c, java.

182
00:06:46,363 --> 00:06:47,055
Zero again.

183
00:06:47,055 --> 00:06:48,249
Nothing is running,

184
00:06:48,249 --> 00:06:49,882
and everything is removed.

185
00:06:49,882 --> 00:06:52,145
Paste these proofs into your report.

186
00:06:54,195 --> 00:06:58,120
Here is how your work is judged. Six points, and you need all six.

187
00:06:58,670 --> 00:07:00,505
The checker shows six pass lines.

188
00:07:01,055 --> 00:07:04,255
Every fault has a symptom, a cause, a fix, and a proof.

189
00:07:04,805 --> 00:07:06,554
You changed one thing at a time.

190
00:07:07,104 --> 00:07:09,920
The report is complete, including where you got stuck.

191
00:07:10,470 --> 00:07:14,246
The cleanup proof shows nothing left behind, and no Java running.

192
00:07:14,796 --> 00:07:17,186
You ran it only in your own virtual machine.

193
00:07:17,736 --> 00:07:19,357
To pass, you need all six.

194
00:07:21,407 --> 00:07:27,274
Your turn, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine. Take your time. Mastery is slow and exact.

195
00:07:27,824 --> 00:07:30,597
One: clone the repository and install the lab.

196
00:07:31,147 --> 00:07:33,963
Two: run lab up, and save the checker output.

197
00:07:34,513 --> 00:07:37,734
Three: fix the three remaining faults, with four notes each.

198
00:07:38,284 --> 00:07:42,252
Four: write report dot text, and the full report from the template.

199
00:07:42,802 --> 00:07:46,002
Five: run the checker. All six lines must say pass.

200
00:07:46,552 --> 00:07:48,515
Six: clean up, and paste the proof.

201
00:07:49,065 --> 00:07:50,900
Pause the video, and begin now.

202
00:08:06,450 --> 00:08:07,325
Quick check.

203
00:08:07,875 --> 00:08:10,243
What does no main manifest attribute mean?

204
00:08:10,793 --> 00:08:13,267
Why do the tests run before the jar is built?

205
00:08:13,817 --> 00:08:15,737
Which option raises the heap limit?

206
00:08:16,287 --> 00:08:17,845
What proves your cleanup worked?

207
00:08:18,395 --> 00:08:21,318
Mastery evidence covered: M C zero nine,

208
00:08:21,318 --> 00:08:23,510
Java fundamentals for dev ops,

209
00:08:23,510 --> 00:08:25,264
objectives one to eight.

210
00:08:25,814 --> 00:08:27,883
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

211
00:08:38,433 --> 00:08:40,289
Next masterclass: Maven.

